PATCH 502: the dead-player cockpit overlay 8568 dereferenced the player near offset as a host pointer.

asm 0x18568-0x185bf (DS=DGROUP=0x1c00), reached from the event drain 206f -> 209e -> 7fb5 once the
player object has been destroyed:
    18568: bb ae 90        mov bx,0x90ae
    1856b: b8 08 05        mov ax,0x508
    1856e: ff 1e b4 06     lcall [0x6b4]
    18572: 8b 3e 34 6d     mov di,[0x6d34]           ; the PLAYER's DGROUP NEAR OFFSET
    18576: f6 85 90 00 80  testb [di+0x90],0x80 ; jne 0x1859e
    1857d: mov bl,[di+0x90] ; xor bh,bh ; shl bx,1
    18585: 8b 87 b8 90     mov ax,[bx-0x6f48]        ; == word[DGROUP:0x90b8 + idx*2]
    18589: push ax ; add [0x90b0],ax ; mov ax,0x510 ; mov bx,0x90ae ; lcall [0x6c8]
    18598: pop ax ; sub [0x90b0],ax ; lret
    1859e: mov ax,[0x90b6] ; add [0x90b0],ax ; addw [0x90ae],2
    185aa: push ax ; mov ax,0x518 ; mov bx,0x90ae ; lcall [0x6c8]
    185b5: pop ax ; sub [0x90b0],ax ; subw [0x90ae],2 ; lret

Three defects: DAT_2000_2d34 holds the player's NEAR OFFSET (patch 300 stores it that way) and was
dereferenced as a host pointer; the -0x6f48 table was read as raw host memory with 4-byte `int`
elements where the asm reads WORDs; and both far calls lost their (ax,bx) argument pair.

Unreachable until patches 499/500/501 let the player-death sequence run to completion; then AZER1
SIGSEGV'd here at 8568 <- 7fb5 <- 209e <- 206f <- 459a.
